<title>BELGIUM: Sugar panel to fix syrup, product refunds.</title>
<headline>Sugar panel to fix syrup, product refunds.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's sugar management committee will on Wednesday fix end of month refunds on syrups and on non-annex II sugar products, EU sources said.</p>
<p>Non-annex II products include biscuits, chocolate and other food items not covered by the Common Agricultural Policy.</p>
<p>&quot;There are no policy issues on the agenda,&quot; said a source, adding the main item will be the weekly white sugar export tender.</p>
<p>The committee will also review import duties on cane molasses and revise the reference price on imports of beet molasses.</p>
</text>
